 cell phone  and i need your help with a very urgent  google search  now i don't know about you guys but when  a stranger calls my house asking me to  search for drugs i obviously do it  wanting more answers chloe devises a new  scheme  taking her mother out to the movies and  pretending to go to the washroom but  then  bolting to the pharmacy across the  street to ask what the hell these pills  are for  sorry everyone cutting through i'm  paralyzed feel bad for me bonus points  if you notice the name of the film  they're seeing is breka which is kind of  fun because she's trying to break out  for most of the movie  turns out the pills were prescribed by a  veterinarian as a muscle relaxant for a  dog they don't even own  but diane has been giving them to her  daughter making it so she can't walk but  then i'm like how did the mom get a  prescription for an animal narcotic when  they don't  have a dog our vets allowed to give out  narcotics without actually seeing the  patient  i don't know so anyway chloe has an  asthma attack and wakes up  locked in her room then there's this  weird scene where diane takes a shower  and she has all these scars over her  back and we're like oh  how did she get those scars we'll  probably find out later but nope they're  never brought up again there's also  another scene where diane writes an  email to chloe's doctor about how her  new medication  is giving her delusions then i'm like  why are you writing to your  doctor when you know that she's not  delusional at all you know you've been  giving her dog  drugs anyway diane has to run some  errands and chloe devises an elaborate  plan to break out of her room  chloe is good with engineering stuff so  hold on let me take a big gasp of air  here she fills her mouth with water  takes a bunch of extension cord climbs  out her window over to her mother's  window uses some sort of engineering  heater thing to crack the glass  then spits the cold water on the hot  spot to smash it open  not gonna lie i thought this was really  ingenuitive and i haven't seen it done  in other movies but at the same time i'm  like  why didn't she just break the glass why  did she go through all this trouble when  she could have just  smashed it open anyway chloe is able to  escape a flag down the mailman but it  just so happens her mom conveniently  arrives at the same time ultimately  knocking him out with a syringe she  always seems to have on hand oh yeah she  later kills him diane ends up chaining  chloe in her wheelchair in the basement  where she's conveniently left out a  whole bunch of stuff she'd never want  chloe to see  in plain sight and a lot of it just  doesn't make any sense  for example chloe has been anxiously  awaiting on acceptance letters from  various colleges  instead of the mom disposing them she  puts them in plain sight in the basement  there's also this shoe box right in the  open next to the tv  that contains all these damning  documents that prove  chloe isn't diane's child and that diane  stole her from another couple years ago  when her  own daughter died and i'm not really  sure why she go through the effort of  clipping out a newspaper article of this  it just doesn't make sense to me so  diane comes downstairs shocked that  chloe has found all these things and i'm  like dude  you're the one who left her down here  with this stuff and i kid you not she  makes a syringe cocktail out of paint  thinner  no i'm no nurse ratchet you put that in  her she's gonna die  and that's not what diane wants she just  wants to keep her daughter forever and  ever so chloe knowing her death is  imminent  chugs a bottle of poisonous  organophosphate like you do  in the hopes her mom will call to get  her to the hospital and that's exactly  what happens as we venture into the  final act of the film  chloe can't speak anymore because of her  poison chug so she has to tell the nurse  what happened via crayon  at this point they think she's suicidal  so no sharp objects like pens for her  and diane knowing any second she could  be caught whisks chloe away when all the  other doctors and nurses are busy with a  code blue now it looks like diane is  gonna get away with it until she's  stopped by a set of stairs not being  wheelchair accessible  oh the irony and we could get into a  whole discussion about how living with a  disability is like having a murderous  overbearing mother who limits what you  can do  but that's an idea for a different video  with nowhere to go diane is  shot by the armed hospital guards i'm  from canada so our hospital security  guards are only armed with maple syrup  flavored pepper spray  so this was a shock to me and here is  where i want to talk about some changes  that could have improved this movie and  where you write in the comments about  how wrong i am in the real version diane  falls after being shot and we see her at  the bottom of the stairs then fast  forward seven years where chloe visits  her in the infirmary at the department  of corrections she can kind of walk now  too  i think the movie missed an awesome  ironic ending if it were to be revealed  that it's now  diane in a wheelchair her bones having  been shattered after falling down  all those stairs like it would have been  awesome for chloe to wheel diane around  their roles having been reversed  instead we get this zany stinger ending  where chloe's been hiding these green  pills in her mouth like maybe even her  stomach and she tells her mother to open  wide well that's the ending i also think  the way the movie started wasn't that  great either the opening scene is sarah  paulson going into labor hinting that  she's gonna lose her child if it were me  i'd cut all that out because  viewers are smart enough to realize  something's up and that chloe probably  isn't her real baby this also takes away  precious screen time that could have  been devoted to making us care about the  protagonist and here i think the writers  did a 